# node2's own settings for qv4-radiance (read by the unit's EnvironmentFile; 12 November 2026, Arthur: "move it").
# The n-gram table is read from the model copy on the spare drive (nvme0n1p2, ext4, label ssd2, mounted at /mnt/ssd2
# with the container file label), not held in host RAM: about 48 GB of RAM back. Measured 12 November 08:44-10:13 on
# the real judgment summaries: 0 to 9% slower than RAM at 1 to 8 at once, 7k-24k reads a second, no collapse. Never
# the copy on /home (btrfs, 2,463 pieces): read from there the drive fell to about 1,000 reads a second.
# The copy was compared byte for byte with /home's model on 12 November.
QV4_RADIANCE_MODEL=/mnt/ssd2/radiance/qwen3.8-next-flash-fp8-iq4r-moe.rad
QV4_RADIANCE_NGRAM=disk
